author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Focused tests tolerate measured Windows external-work latency without raising global suite timeouts; temporary Git/merge resources are closed before cleanup and EBUSY cleanup is retried in a bounded portable helper; the full Windows Node 24 nightly passes; the GitHub issue links this PM item.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "windows-latest, Node 24, scheduled Nightly Validation run 30246735868"
repro_steps: Run the full nightly test command on Windows Node 24 at f4817e0; observe extension-command.spec.ts line 1604 timeout and merge-safety.spec.ts temp cleanup EBUSY.
resolution: Raised the Windows-sensitive external-work timeout to 60 seconds and hardened merge cleanup with bounded EBUSY-style retries.
expected_result: Nightly Windows verification tolerates realistic installation and filesystem latency without masking genuine hangs.
actual_result: "The regression uses an explicit 60-second timeout, cleanup retries are bounded, and cross-platform-focused plus full suites pass."
affected_version: 2026.7.27
component: Windows nightly test reliability
regression: true
customer_impact: A red nightly weakens release confidence even though all product assertions pass.
